examples.solution_text:
Draw touching columns of width $1$, centred at each score. Their heights are $3,6,0,8,4$; score $3$ has no visible column.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.45cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {Score};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,9) node[above] {$f$};
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.12);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\h in {1/3,2/6,4/8,5/4} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The tallest column is centred at score $4$, so the mode is $4$.

