examples.solution_text:
Join the centres of the column tops, including $(4,0)$. Extend the polygon to the empty score at each end: $(1,0)$ and $(6,0)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=0.45cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{semanticRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,9) node[above] {$f$};
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.12);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\h in {2/5,3/7,5/3} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);}
\draw[semanticRed,thick] (1,0)--(2,5)--(3,7)--(4,0)--(5,3)--(6,0);
\foreach \p in {(1,0),(2,5),(3,7),(4,0),(5,3),(6,0)} {\fill[semanticRed] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Draw touching columns centred at scores $2$ to $6$, with cumulative heights $4,7,7,12,16$. Join the top-right corners, starting at $(1.5,0)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.25cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{semanticRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {Score};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,18) node[above] {$cf$};
\foreach \y in {0,4,8,12,16} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\v/\h in {1/2/4,2/3/7,3/4/7,4/5/12,5/6/16} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.2);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.2) {$\v$};}
\draw[semanticRed,thick] (0.5,0)--(1.5,4)--(2.5,7)--(3.5,7)--(4.5,12)--(5.5,16);
\foreach \p in {(0.5,0),(1.5,4),(2.5,7),(3.5,7),(4.5,12),(5.5,16)} {\fill[semanticRed] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The ogive is horizontal across the column for score $4$ because its frequency is $0$. Its cumulative column still has height $7$.

examples.question_text:
The cumulative frequency histogram and ogive show ungrouped test scores. Find the median score.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.18cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{semanticRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {Score};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,27) node[above] {$cf$};
\foreach \y in {0,6,12,18,24} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\v/\h in {1/6/3,2/7/8,3/8/17,4/9/21,5/10/24} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\v$};}
\draw[semanticRed,thick] (0.5,0)--(1.5,3)--(2.5,8)--(3.5,17)--(4.5,21)--(5.5,24);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The final cumulative frequency gives $n=24$.

$\begin{aligned}0.5\times n&=0.5\times24\\&=12\end{aligned}$

Draw a horizontal line at $cf=12$ to the ogive.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.18cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{semanticRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{semanticBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {Score};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,27) node[above] {$cf$};
\foreach \y in {0,6,12,18,24} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\v/\h in {1/6/3,2/7/8,3/8/17,4/9/21,5/10/24} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\v$};}
\draw[semanticRed,thick] (0.5,0)--(1.5,3)--(2.5,8)--(3.5,17)--(4.5,21)--(5.5,24);
\draw[semanticBlue,dashed,thick] (0,12)--(2.944444,12);
\fill[semanticBlue] (2.944444,12) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The intersection lies in the column for score $8$, where cumulative frequency rises from $8$ to $17$. Both middle observations, positions $12$ and $13$, have score $8$. The median is $8$; an interpolated boundary reading is not the ungrouped score.
